					<dc:identifier>http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1984/458/contents/made</dc:identifier><dc:title>The Social Security Adjudication (Consequential Amendments) Regulations 1984</dc:title><dc:publisher>Westlaw</dc:publisher><dc:publisher>King's Printer of Acts of Parliament</dc:publisher><dc:modified>2011-04-05</dc:modified><dc:subject scheme="SIheading">SOCIAL SECURITY INDUSTRIAL TRIBUNALS</dc:subject>
					<dc:description>These regulations make amendments consequential on the passing
of the Health and Social Services and Social
Security Adjudications Act 1983 and the making
of the Social Security (Adjudication) Regulations
1984 to various regulations made under the
Social Security, Child Benefit, Supplementary Benefits, and Family Income
Supplements Acts.</dc:description>
